'' See the source's header. fbc compiles this and prints '11  21' -- measured on
'' 1.20.0 -- from the direct call and through the pointer both.
''
'' The result type is the assertion that matters as much as the absence of the error:
'' with the definition judged against the TYPE rather than against its own class, the
'' function came out as 'func ptr FN' -- the alias's type, not its own.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/typename-and-proc-share-a-name.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: func i32 FN(i32
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var ptr p = FN
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0600
'' EXPECT-NOT: func ptr FN
